    <heading level="1">Section 7.1 Exercises</heading>
    <heading level="1">Practice Makes Perfect</heading>
    <paragraph>Determine the Values for Which a Rational Expression is Undefined</paragraph>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, determine the values for which the rational expression is undefined.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="1" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$\frac{2x^{2}}{z}$$ , ⓑ $$\frac{4p - 1}{6p - 5}$$ , ⓒ $$\frac{n - 3}{n^{2} + 2n - 8}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$z=0z=0$$ ⓑ $$p=56p=56$$ ⓒ $$n=-4,n=2n=-4,n=2$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="2" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$\frac{10m}{11n}$$ , ⓑ $$\frac{6y + 13}{4y - 9}$$ , ⓒ $$\frac{b - 8}{b^{2} - 36}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="3" has_solution="true">
